#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:28
msgid "Role changes are saved automatically, there is no need to manually save"
msgstr ""
"Rol changes are saved automatically, there is no need to manually save"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:30
msgid ""
"Additionally, users should have a Linux and/or Windows username and "
"password configured in their user profiles in order for virtual desktop "
"login to be as seamless as possible. User profiles are accessed by "
"clicking on the user's name in the upper-right corner of the application "
"windows and clicking USER SETTINGS. The section to enter Windows and "
"Linux account credentials is in the right column of the page."
msgstr ""
"Adicionalmente, users should have a Linux and/or Windows username and "
"password configurado en their user profiles in order for escritorio "
"virtual login to be as seamless as possible. User profiles are accessed by "
"clicking on the user's name in the upper-right corner of the application "
"windows and clicking USER SETTINGS. The section to enter Windows and Linux "
"account credentials is in the right column of the page."

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:33
msgid "Creating VDI Templates"
msgstr "Crear plantillas VDI"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:35
msgid ""
"The following guide focuses on VMware and Windows but is applicable to "
"most cloud environments. |morpheus| also supports Linux virtual desktops."
msgstr ""
"Lo siguiente guide focuses on VMware and Windows but is applicable to most "
"cloud environments. |morpheus| also supports Linux virtual desktops."

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:37
msgid ""
"Create a thin-provisioned VM in the VMware vCenter console. It's "
"recommended you allocate at least 50 GB of storage, at least 2 vCPU and "
"at least 8 GB RAM on the template. Smaller VMs can be deployed from this "
"template later."
msgstr ""
"Create a thin-provisioned VM in the VMware vCenter console. It's "
"recommended you allocate at least 50 GB of storage, at least 2 vCPU and at "
"least 8 GB RAM on the template. Smaller VMs puede ser deployed from this "
"template later."

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:38
msgid ""
"Install a Windows operating system, there is no need to supply a license "
"during deployment."
msgstr ""
"Install a Windows operating system, there es no need a supply a license "
"durante deployment."

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:39
msgid "Supply the initial username and password"
msgstr "Proporcione el nombre de usuario y contraseña inicial"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:40
msgid ""
"Install any updates, applications or optimizations. See the next section "
"for recommended optimizations for the most performant virtual desktop "
"experience"
msgstr ""
"Install any updates, applications or optimizations. See the next section "
"for recommended optimizations for the most performant escritorio virtual "
"experience"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:41
msgid ""
"Shutdown the VM and convert to a template. Optionally, you can also use "
"the Linked Clones (VMware) process which is described in a later section"
msgstr ""
"Shutdown the VM and convert to a template. Optionally, you can also use "
"the Linked Clones (VMware) process which is descrito en a later section"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:44
msgid "Suggested Optimizations"
msgstr "Optimizaciones sugeridas"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:46
msgid ""
"Reducing display and input delays is key to providing the best virtual "
"desktop experience for the user. Consider the following optimizations for"
" VDI desktops and servers:"
msgstr ""
"Reducing display and input delays is key to providing the best virtual "
"desktop experience for the user. Consider lo siguiente optimizations for "
"VDI desktops and servers:"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:48
msgid "Disable desktop wallpapers"
msgstr "Desactivar fondos de pantalla del escritorio"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:49
msgid "Implement Roaming Profiles"
msgstr "Implementar Perfiles Itinerantes"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:50
msgid "Enforce WDDM remote display driver"
msgstr "Forzar controlador de pantalla remota WDDM"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:51
msgid "Re-enable local Administrator"
msgstr "Rehabilitar el Administrador local"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:52
msgid "Delete the initial created user profile"
msgstr "Eliminar el perfil de usuario creado inicialmente"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:53
msgid "Clean up any unneeded installer packages"
msgstr "Limpiar paquetes de instalador innecesarios"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:55
msgid ""
"Additionally, there are a number of OS optimization tools available on "
"the Internet which are specific to VDI use cases."
msgstr ""
"Adicionalmente, there are a number of OS optimization tools available on "
"the Internet which are specific to VDI use cases."

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:58
msgid "Linked Clones"
msgstr "Clones vinculados"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:60
msgid ""
"Linked Clones are a feature of VMware which references snapshots of a VM "
"to deploy from. This adds the advantage of quicker clone times and the "
"ability to more easily share small modifications to a file system. "
"|morpheus| supports Linked Clones but recommends them for VDI workloads "
"only."
msgstr ""
"Linked Clones are a función of VMware which references snapshots of a VM "
"to deploy from. This adds the advantage of quicker clone times and the "
"ability to more easily share small modifications to a file system. "
"|morpheus| supports Linked Clones but recommends them for VDI workloads "
"only."

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:62
msgid "Linked Clones are not templates but rather powered down VMs."
msgstr "Linked Clones son no templates but rather powered down VMs."

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:64
msgid ""
"Locate the VM you desire to have the Linked Clone in |morpheus|. If it's "
"not currently managed by |morpheus|, navigate to the appropriate Cloud "
"(Infrastructure > Clouds), find the VM on the \"VMs\" tab, and click "
"\"Convert to Managed\" from the ACTIONS menu"
msgstr ""
"Locate the VM you desire to have the Linked Clone in |morpheus|. If it's "
"not currently administrado por |morpheus|, navegue a the appropriate Cloud "
"(Infrastructure > Clouds), find the VM on the \"VMs\" tab, and click "
"\"Convert to Managed\" from the ACTIONS menu"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:65
msgid ""
"In the CONVERT TO INSTANCE modal, select \"No Agent Install\" in the "
"AGENT field"
msgstr ""
"In the CONVERT TO INSTANCE modal, select \"No Agent Install\" in the AGENT "
"campo"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:66
msgid ""
"If snapshots are already on the VM, these will now be synced by "
"|morpheus|. If you have not yet created a snapshot, do so in the vCenter "
"console (and refresh the Cloud integration in |morpheus| afterward) or "
"from the ACTIONS menu in |morpheus| itself. Be sure to take a snapshot of"
" a powered-off VM and give the snapshot a name that will be identifiable "
"for administrators"
msgstr ""
"If snapshots are already on the VM, these will now be synced by "
"|morpheus|. If you have not yet created a snapshot, do so in the vCenter "
"console (and refresh the Cloud integration in |morpheus| afterward) or "
"from the ACTIONS menu in |morpheus| itself. Be sure to take a snapshot of "
"a powered-off VM and give the snapshot a name that será identifiable for "
"administrators"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:67
msgid ""
"From the Instance detail page in |morpheus|, navigate to the Backups tab "
"to find the snapshot"
msgstr ""
"From the Instance detail page in |morpheus|, navegue a the Backups tab to "
"find the snapshot"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:68
msgid "Select \"More\" and create the Linked Clone"
msgstr "Seleccione \"More\" y create el/la Linked Clone"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:69
msgid ""
"The Linked Clone will now appear in the |morpheus| Virtual Image "
"repository (|LibVir|), ready to use with your custom Layouts"
msgstr ""
"El Linked Clone se now appear en el/la |morpheus| Virtual Image repository "
"(|LibVir|), ready a use con your custom Layouts"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:71
msgid ""
"You should modify the Virtual Image to \"Force Guest Customization\" "
"unless you ``sysprep`` your VM at shutdown time"
msgstr ""
"You should modify el/la Virtual Image a \"Force Guest Customization\" "
"unless you ``sysprep`` your VM en shutdown time"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:74
msgid "Creating or Editing a VDI Pool"
msgstr "Crear o editar un Pool VDI"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:76
msgid ""
"VDI pools are configured from the Tools menu (VDI Pools selection). The "
"following information is displayed in the VDI pools list view, bear in "
"mind some fields may be hidden depending on how you've configured your "
"VDI pools list view (gear icon):"
msgstr ""
"VDI pools are configured from the Tools menu (VDI Pools selection). Lo "
"siguiente information is displayed in the VDI pools list view, bear in "
"mind some fields puede ser hidden depending on how you've configured your "
"VDI pools list view (gear icon):"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:78
msgid ""
"**TYPE:** An icon indicating the machine type associated with the pool. "
"|morpheus| includes many logos out of the box and also allows users to "
"set their own custom icons"
msgstr ""
"**TYPE:** An icon indicating the machine type asociado con the pool. "
"|morpheus| includes many logos out of the box and also permite a los "
"usuarios set their own custom icons"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:79
msgid "**NAME:** The friendly name given to the VDI pool"
msgstr "**NAME:** The friendly nombre given to the VDI pool"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:80
msgid ""
"**PERSISTENT:** A check mark will appear when the VDI pool is configured "
"for persistent virtual desktops"
msgstr ""
"**PERSISTENT:** A check mark will appear when the VDI pool está "
"configurado for persistent escritorio virtuals"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:81
msgid ""
"**ENABLED:** A check mark will appear when the VDI pool is enabled and "
"visible to users whose Role permissions allow them access"
msgstr ""
"**ENABLED:** A check mark will appear when the VDI pool está habilitado "
"and visible to users whose Role permissions allow them access"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:82
msgid ""
"**POOL USAGE:** A graph representing the usage of the VDI pool. The total"
" length of the bar represents the maximum pool size based on the "
"configuration. Green segments represent available virtual desktops, blue "
"segments represent reserved virtual desktops, yellow segments represent "
"virtual desktops which are being prepared, and gray segments represent "
"additional pool capacity which could be made available depending on how "
"many virtual desktops are currently reserved and how many idle machines "
"you've configured the pool to keep available"
msgstr ""
"**POOL USAGE:** A graph representing the usage of the VDI pool. The total "
"length of the bar represents the maximum pool size based on the "
"configuration. Green segments represent available escritorio virtuals, "
"blue segments represent reserved escritorio virtuals, yellow segments "
"represent escritorio virtuals which are being prepared, and gray segments "
"represent additional pool capacity which could be made available "
"dependiendo de how many escritorio virtuals are currently reserved and how "
"many idle machines you've configured the pool to keep available"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:83
msgid "**DESCRIPTION:** A description of the virtual desktop type, if provided"
msgstr ""
"**DESCRIPTION:** A description of the escritorio virtual type, if provided"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:86
msgid ".. image:: images/personas/vdi/vdiPools.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/personas/vdi/vdiPools.png"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:87
msgid ""
"Create a VDI pool by selecting :guilabel:`+ ADD` from the VDI Pools tab "
"or edit an existing one by clicking on the pencil icon from the "
"appropriate row. Configure the following, fields containing a vertical "
"blue bar along the left edge are required:"
msgstr ""
"Create a VDI pool by selecting :guilabel:`+ ADD` from the VDI Pools tab or "
"edit an existing one by clicking on the pencil icon from the appropriate "
"row. Configure lo siguiente, fields containing a vertical blue bar along "
"the left edge son requeridos:"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:89
msgid "**NAME:** A friendly name for the VDI pool in |morpheus|"
msgstr "**NAME:** A friendly nombre for the VDI pool in |morpheus|"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:90
msgid "**DESCRIPTION:** A description of the virtual desktop type"
msgstr "**DESCRIPTION:** A description of the escritorio virtual type"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:91
msgid ""
"**MIN IDLE:** The minimum number of virtual desktops that should remain "
"idle and ready"
msgstr ""
"**MIN IDLE:** The minimum number of escritorio virtuals that should remain "
"idle and ready"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:92
msgid ""
"**INITIAL POOL SIZE:** The number of virtual desktops that will be "
"prepared when the pool is created or enabled"
msgstr ""
"**INITIAL POOL SIZE:** The number of virtual desktops that será prepared "
"when the pool is created or enabled"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:93
msgid ""
"**MAX IDLE:** The maximum number of virtual desktops that remain idle and"
" ready. Machines will be shut down as necessary when this number is "
"exceeded due to users vacating their machines"
msgstr ""
"**MAX IDLE:** The maximum number of virtual desktops that remain idle and "
"ready. Machines será shut down as necessary when this number is exceeded "
"due to users vacating their machines"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:94
msgid ""
"**MAX SIZE:** The total number of virtual desktops this pool can have. "
"Additional users will not be able to access machines once this number is "
"reached"
msgstr ""
"**MAX SIZE:** The total number of escritorio virtuals this pool can have. "
"Additional users will not be able to access machines once this number is "
"reached"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:95
msgid ""
"**LEASE TIMEOUT (MINUTES):** The user lease time on a virtual desktop "
"they've reserved. The lease will continue to auto-renew itself as long as"
" the user is logged into |morpheus|. Once the user has logged out and the"
" lease timeout period has expired, the machine will be released as "
"appropriate based on your configuration"
msgstr ""
"**LEASE TIMEOUT (MINUTES):** The user lease time on a virtual desktop "
"they've reserved. The lease will continue to auto-renew itself as long as "
"the user is logged into |morpheus|. Once the user has logged out and the "
"lease timeout period has expired, the machine será released as appropriate "
"based on your configuration"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:96
msgid ""
"**PERSISTENT:** Pools with persistent virtual desktops will reserve a "
"machine for each user in order to preserve settings, installed "
"applications, work files and more. Machines in persistent pools will be "
"shut down rather than destroyed when they are no longer in use"
msgstr ""
"**PERSISTENT:** Pools with persistent virtual desktops will reserve a "
"machine for each user para preserve settings, installed applications, work "
"files and more. Machines in persistent pools será shut down rather than "
"destroyed when they are no longer in use"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:97
msgid ""
"**RECYCLABLE:** When enabled, the VDI Instance will revert back to a "
"snapshot and become available once again after the user has logged out "
"and the VDI session has expired. This behavior will not apply to VDI "
"pools which are also configured to be persistent because in that "
"configuration the Instance is merely stopped and saved for the user's "
"next session. This feature is currently only available for Cloud types "
"which support snapshot management (VMware, Nutanix, and vCD)"
msgstr ""
"**RECYCLABLE:** Cuando está habilitado, the VDI Instance will revert back "
"to a snapshot and become available once again after the user has logged "
"out and the VDI session has expired. This behavior will not apply to VDI "
"pools which are also configured to be persistent because in that "
"configuration the Instance is merely stopped and saved for the user's next "
"session. This feature is currently only available for Cloud types which "
"support snapshot management (VMware, Nutanix, and vCD)"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:98
msgid ""
"**ALLOW COPY** Enables or disables the ability for the VDI user to copy "
"contents from the VDI instance to the local clipboard"
msgstr ""
"**ALLOW COPY** Enables or disables the ability for the VDI usuario to copy "
"contents from the VDI instancia to the local clipboard"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:99
msgid ""
"**ALLOW PRINTER** When enabled, users local system printers can be "
"targeted from the VDI Instance"
msgstr ""
"**ALLOW PRINTER** When enabled, users local system printers puede ser "
"targeted from the VDI Instance"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:100
msgid ""
"**ALLOW HYPERVISOR CONSOLE:** When checked, native cloud console will be "
"enabled (if available) rather than using |morpheus|-native RDP/SSH "
"capability"
msgstr ""
"**ALLOW HYPERVISOR CONSOLE:** When checked, native cloud console será "
"enabled (if available) rather than using |morpheus|-native RDP/SSH "
"capability"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:101
msgid ""
"**AUTO CREATE LOCAL USER UPON RESERVATION:** When marked, the user "
"configured in |morpheus| user settings will be created when the machine "
"is initially accessed. If unchecked or if there is no user configured in "
"|morpheus| user settings, ensure the machine is joining a domain or there"
" is a known user on the machine image in order to allow access"
msgstr ""
"**AUTO CREATE LOCAL USER UPON RESERVATION:** When marked, the user "
"configured in |morpheus| user settings será created when the machine is "
"initially accessed. If unchecked or if there is no user configured in "
"|morpheus| user settings, ensure the machine is joining a domain or there "
"is a known user on the machine image para allow access"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:102
msgid ""
"**ENABLED:** When marked, the initial pool size will begin to deploy once"
" the VDI pool is saved. The icon for this desktop environment will also "
"be presented to Virtual Desktop Persona users"
msgstr ""
"**ENABLED:** When marked, the initial pool size serágin to deploy once the "
"VDI pool is saved. The icon for this desktop environment will also be "
"presented to Virtual Desktop Persona users"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:103
msgid ""
"**CONFIGURE:** Click this button to configure the deployment "
"configuration each system will use. The wizard is identical to the "
"Instance provisioning wizard meaning all available Instance Types, "
"Workflows, and more are available to virtual desktop machine creation. "
"Consult the steps above to see an example VDI image prep walkthrough"
msgstr ""
"**CONFIGURE:** Click this button to configure the deployment configuration "
"each system will use. The wizard is identical to the Instance provisioning "
"wizard meaning all available Instance Types, Workflows, and more están "
"disponibles to virtual desktop machine creation. Consult the steps above "
"to see an example VDI image prep walkthrough"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:104
msgid ""
"**LOGO:** Upload or select a logo to represent the virtual desktop type "
"to users"
msgstr ""
"**LOGO:** Upload or select a logo to represent the escritorio virtual type "
"to users"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:105
msgid ""
"**VDI APPS:** Optionally select one or more frequently-used applications "
"the user can launch directly. Users will also have the option to launch "
"into the desktop"
msgstr ""
"**VDI APPS:** Optionally select one or more frequently-used applications "
"the usuario can launch directly. Usuarios will also have the opción to "
"launch into the desktop"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:106
msgid ""
"**VDI GATEWAY** Select a configure VDI Gateway for VDI sessions to be "
"redirected to. VDI sessions will be redirected to the gateway when a "
"gateway is specified."
msgstr ""
"**VDI GATEWAY** Select a configure VDI Gateway for VDI sessions to be "
"redirected to. VDI sessions será redirected to the gateway when a gateway "
"is specified."

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:109
msgid "**Guest Console SSH Tunnel** (optional)"
msgstr "**Guest Console SSH Tunnel** (opcional)"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:109
